  provenance: "PROVISIONAL L1 SEMANTIC LAYER - not a final claim about the specimen.\n\nDERIVED
    FROM SW_A1_L1_BladeProfile on 2026-08-19, NOT authored independently.\n\nWhy
    transfer rather than re-author: A1 and B1 are the same blade construction with\n
    specimen-specific dimensions. Semantics are shared; geometry is specimen-specific.\n
    Re-declaring B1's cutting edges from scratch would invite an inconsistency between\n
    two specimens that are the same design.\n\nWhat transferred UNCHANGED (semantics):\n
    Both long edge polylines -> SharpEdge, at Across +/-0.0225.\n  Blade flats, bevels
    and centreline -> non-cutting.\n  Ring topology, all 12 vertices per station,
    every RidgeType and FacetType.\n  Cap types: StartCapType Unresolved, EndCapType
    Tip.\n Cross-section coordinates (Across, Through) are byte-identical to A1,
    because the\n two specimens share width 0.045 m and thickness 0.005 m exactly,
    as measured from\n their cooked blade collider bounds.\n\nWhat was RESCALED (geometry):\n 
    Station Along values only, by the ratio of the two specimens' measured blade
    spans.\n  A1 span -0.010693 -> -1.026693 = 1.016000 m (matches its collider bounds
    exactly).\n B1 span -0.010695 -> -1.020705 = 1.010010 m (matches its collider
    bounds exactly).\n ratio = 1.010010 / 1.016000 = 0.9941043. The guard-end stations
    differ by 2 um;\n the difference is essentially all at the tip, 6 mm shorter.\n\nKNOWN
    LIMITATION, carried deliberately:\n  The authored basis (bladeAxis, edgeAxis,
    faceNormal) is TRANSFERRED FROM A1 and was NOT\n  independently derived from
    B1's own quillon and tip markers. A1's bladeAxis carries a\n  1.24 degree tilt
    off local -X from its own marker fit; B1's true tilt has not been\n  measured.
    Both blades sit identically in their prefabs (Blade child localPosition\n  (0,
    -0.002533, 0), collider centre y 0.00253), so the assumption is reasonable, but
    it\n  IS an assumption. Derive B1's basis from B1's markers before any quantitative
    claim\n  depends on the edge direction.\n\n  bladeAxis (local) = (-0.999767,
    0.021566, 0.000000)   [from A1]\n edgeAxis  (local) = (0.000000, 0.000000, 1.000000)  
    [from A1]\n  faceNormal(local) = (0.021566, 0.999767, 0.000000)   [from A1]\n\nBOTH
    long edges are designated SharpEdge, so classification is invariant to the sign
    of\nedgeAxis, exactly as for A1."
